title: The Constituent Assembly Election
subtitle: [? if assembly_early = 1 : The election, brought forward to October. ?][? if assembly_early = 0 : The election of 25 November. ?]
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: (assembly_early = 0 and dix >= 21) or (assembly_early = 1 and dix >= 19)
priority: 45
max-visits: 1

= The Constituent Assembly Election

[? if assembly_early = 1 : The Provisional Government, under pressure from the Soviet, brought the elections forward. ?][? if assembly_early = 0 : The elections to the Constituent Assembly, postponed twice by the Provisional Government, have been held in the middle of a revolution. ?] Voting took place over several weeks, in 70 electoral districts. The election was the freest in Russia's history: some 44 million people voted.

[? if player_party = 'menshevik' : The Mensheviks cannot count on the villages. The SRs will win the peasants, the Bolsheviks the capitals and the northern front, the national parties their regions. Our votes are in the towns, among the railwaymen, in Georgia. The question is whether to run alone. ?][? if player_party = 'sr' : The SRs will win the peasants. The Bolsheviks will win the capitals and the northern front, the national parties their regions. The Mensheviks are a party of the towns and of Georgia. The party's own lists carry the unity of the Left SRs and the Right: for now. The question is whether to run alone. ?]

- @alone: Run our own lists.
- @joint: Run a joint list with the [+ partner_name +]. (Alliance level 2 or relations of 60 or better.)
- @united: Run a united list of all moderate socialists.
- @lsr_separate: Run separate Left SR lists.

@alone
on-arrival: {!
Q.ca_extra = 0;
!}
go-to: ca_results

@joint
choose-if: ally_lvl >= 2 or rel_ally >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ partner_name +] will not agree to a joint list.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ca_extra = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 2);
!}
go-to: ca_results

@united
choose-if: (ally_lvl >= 2 and (ally_lsr >= 1 or rel_lsr >= 45)) or ally_lvl >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: This needs a bloc with the [+ partner_name +] and relations with the Left SRs.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ca_extra = 2;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 5, rel_lsr: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 3);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 3);
!}
go-to: ca_results

@ca_results
on-arrival: {!
var extra = null;
if (Q.player_party == 'menshevik') {
    if (Q.ca_extra == 1) { extra = {men: 1.7}; }
    if (Q.ca_extra == 2) { extra = {men: 2.4, sr: 1.05}; }
} else if (Q.player_party == 'sr') {
    if (Q.ca_extra == 1) { extra = {sr: 1.04, men: 1.5}; }
    if (Q.ca_extra == 2) { extra = {sr: 1.08, men: 2.0}; }
} else {
    if (Q.ca_extra == 3) { extra = {lsr: 1.3}; }
    if (Q.ca_extra == 1) { extra = {sr: 1.0}; }
}
RO.setResults(Q, 'assembly', extra, 703);
RO.recordParliament(Q, 'assembly', 'The Constituent Assembly');
Q.ca_elected = 1;
Q.ca_moderate = (Q.res_men + Q.res_sr + Q.res_lsr + Q.res_pop + Q.res_nat >= 55) ? 1 : 0;
Q.ca_men_pct = Q.res_men;
if (Q.assembly_early) { RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: -10, soviet_democracy: 2}); }
!}

= The Results

The results, by our count:

{!<div class="parliament" data-name="assembly"></div>!}

[? if player_party = 'sr' : Your party has won more votes than any other party in the history of Russia. ?][? if player_party = 'lsr' and lsr_split = 0 : The Left SRs, who ran on the SR lists, count about [+ res_lsr_in +] percent of the vote, a quarter of the SR delegation. ?][? if player_party = 'lsr' and lsr_split = 1 : The Left SRs, who ran on lists of their own, have [+ res_lsr +] percent of the vote and [+ seat_lsr +] seats. ?][? if ca_moderate = 1 : The moderate socialists and the national parties have a clear majority. The Assembly is theirs, if it meets. ?][? if ca_moderate = 0 : The moderate socialists do not have a majority. The Assembly will be a quarrelsome place. ?]

@lsr_separate
view-if: player_party = 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.ca_extra = 3;
Q.lsr_split = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: -8});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, -2);
!}
go-to: ca_results
